    {
      "title": "Transport Layer Mental Model: Ports, Sockets, TCP vs UDP",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Transport Layer Mental Model: Ports, Sockets, TCP vs UDP",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Layers and Ports",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:IP}: ==host-to-host== delivery",
                "{green:Transport}: ==process-to-process== delivery",
                "Port = **16-bit** number, 0-65535"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Range",
                "Name"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "0-1023",
                  "Well-known"
                ],
                [
                  "1024-49151",
                  "Registered"
                ],
                [
                  "49152-65535",
                  "Ephemeral"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sockets and the 4-tuple",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Socket== = IP address + port",
                "TCP connection = **4-tuple**: src IP, src port, dst IP, dst port",
                "One listening port serves many clients: each connection has a different 4-tuple",
                "Same client IP, ports 50001 and 50002 to server :443 = two connections"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. TCP vs UDP",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "TCP",
                "UDP"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Setup",
                  "Connection-oriented",
                  "Connectionless"
                ],
                [
                  "Delivery",
                  "{green:Reliable}, ordered",
                  "{red:Unreliable}"
                ],
                [
                  "Unit",
                  "Byte stream",
                  "Datagrams"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Port is not connection",
              "text": "A port names a process. Only the ==4-tuple== names a TCP connection."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Port vs socket?** Port picks a process; socket = IP + port.",
                "**One port, many clients?** Each connection has its own 4-tuple.",
                "**TCP vs UDP?** Reliable ordered stream vs unreliable datagrams."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "TCP Handshake and Teardown",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "TCP Handshake and Teardown",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three-Way Handshake",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "SYN",
                    "sub": "client, seq=x",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "SYN-ACK",
                    "sub": "server, seq=y, ack=x+1",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACK",
                    "sub": "client, ack=y+1",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==SYN== and ==FIN== each consume **one sequence number**",
                "True even when the segment carries no data"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Teardown",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "FIN",
                    "note": "active closer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACK",
                    "note": "peer",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "FIN",
                    "note": "peer",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACK",
                    "note": "active closer",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "TIME_WAIT",
                    "note": "2×MSL",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Four steps: each direction closes ==independently== (**half-close**)",
                "Active closer holds ==TIME_WAIT== for **2×MSL** (about 60s)",
                "Why: late packets expire, and the final ACK can be resent"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Abort with RST",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==RST== aborts a connection **immediately**",
                "Sent when a segment arrives for a {red:closed port}",
                "Also sent on a {red:fatal error}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "==TIME_WAIT== sits on the side that closes first (the **active closer**), whether client or server."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sequence Numbers and ACKs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Sequence Numbers and ACKs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Seq and ACK",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Seq== = byte offset of the segment's first data byte, **not** a segment counter",
                "==ACK== = next byte the receiver expects (cumulative acknowledgement)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Sender sends",
                "Receiver replies"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "seq=1000, 500 bytes",
                  "ack=1500 (1000 + 500)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. ISN and Fast Retransmit",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==ISN== is random per connection",
                "Stale packets from an old connection are not accepted as new",
                "Blind spoofing becomes hard to guess",
                "{red:3 duplicate ACKs} → retransmit at once, no wait for the ==RTO=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "title": "Same numbers as the example",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "seq=1500 lost",
                    "note": "500 bytes",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "seq=2000 arrives",
                    "note": "ack=1500",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "seq=2500 arrives",
                    "note": "ack=1500",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "seq=3000 arrives",
                    "note": "ack=1500",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Resend seq=1500",
                    "note": "after 3 dup ACKs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "ACK names the next byte **wanted**, never the last byte received."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Is seq a segment counter?** No, it is a byte offset.",
                "**seq=1000 with 500 bytes: which ack?** ack=1500, the next expected byte.",
                "**Why retransmit on 3 duplicate ACKs?** It signals loss early, skipping the RTO wait."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Flow Control: Sliding Window",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Flow Control: Sliding Window",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Sender's Limit",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Flow control protects the ==receiver==",
                "Receiver puts its free buffer in every ACK as ==rwnd==",
                "`cwnd` = sender's own congestion window, a network-side limit (see congestion control)",
                "In flight ≤ ==min(rwnd, cwnd)== unacknowledged bytes"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sliding and Stalling",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Send",
                    "sub": "up to window",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ACK arrives",
                    "sub": "bytes confirmed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Window slides right",
                    "sub": "left edge moves",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Send new bytes",
                    "sub": "space opened",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:rwnd = 0} stalls the sender",
                "It sends ==zero-window probes== until the receiver reopens the window"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Big Windows",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Window field is 16 bits: max ==65535 bytes==",
                "Too small on high bandwidth-delay links: the pipe never fills",
                "==Window scaling== option: window = field × 2^shift, shift up to ==14=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Two limits",
              "text": "{blue:rwnd} protects the receiver, {orange:cwnd} protects the network. The sender obeys the ==smaller==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Congestion Control: Slow Start and AIMD",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Congestion Control: Slow Start and AIMD",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Limits",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "rwnd",
                "cwnd"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Protects",
                  "receiver (flow control)",
                  "{red:network} (congestion control)"
                ],
                [
                  "Kept by",
                  "receiver, sent in ACKs",
                  "sender, its own"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. cwnd Over Time",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "array",
              "spec": {
                "cells": [
                  "10",
                  "20",
                  "40",
                  "80",
                  "81",
